ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sch1nken/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T15:44:04Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T15:46:20Z","body":"Can confirm on my setup.\n`Godot v4.4.1.stable - Manjaro Linux #1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Wed, 26 Mar 2025 07:48:57 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon Graphics (radeonsi, renoir, ACO, DRM 3.61, 6.14.0-1-MANJARO) - AMD Ryzen 7 4800H with Radeon Graphics (16 threads)`\n\nApart from the non-uniformly scaled collision shapes (which can lead to issues) I couldn't find anything particular wrong with it. \n\nChanging to Jolt Physics though shows no issues. So I'd suspect it has something to do with GodotPhysics.\nI separated the three lines of code into separate functions so the profiler picks them up and the lags come from `move_and_slide()`.\n\nAlso changing the CollisionShape3D on the `Fan` scenes to a CapsuleShape3D improves performance considerably (from about 800ms to ~4ms).\n\nEdit: Can also confirm on 4.4","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783813558/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]